@model bool
@* Why the public demo is read-only and has no sign-up (Sprint 17, S17-4). Collapsed on Sign in;
   Register passes true to show it open. *@
@{
    var open = Model;
}
<details class="dfh-demo-why" open="@(open ? "open" : null)">
    <summary>Why read-only? Why no sign-up?</summary>
    <ul>
        <li>This demo is public and shared by everyone, so uploads, edits and new accounts are blocked. Every visitor sees the same sample data.</li>
        <li>The data is reset when the server restarts. The free server sleeps when idle, so the first visit can take a minute.</li>
        <li>Generating new AI summaries is turned off because every request costs money. The summaries and comparisons you see were saved in advance.</li>
        <li>
            To upload files and use your own account, run your own copy:
            <code>dotnet run --project src/DocFlowHub.Web</code>
            (<a href="https://github.com/bartoszclapinski/Doc-Flow-Hub#running-it-locally" rel="noopener">instructions on GitHub</a>).
        </li>
    </ul>
</details>
